{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-2740"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of electric lighting equipment"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "2740"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :electric-lighting/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :product-safety :consumer-electrical-safety :photobiological-safety]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :electric-lighting-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :eda :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "ElecLightingAdvisor ⊣ Electric Lighting Plant Operations Governor,
 langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A plant OPERATIONS
 COORDINATION actor for electric-lighting-equipment manufacturing
 (LED/lamp-assembly, fixture-housing/optics-assembly, and photometric/
 electrical testing lines producing finished LED lamps, LED
 luminaires, LED drivers, downlight fixtures, and street-light
 fixtures) -- not direct assembly/test-bench-equipment control
 authority and not electric-lighting-equipment-safety-certification
 authority (e.g. UL/CE compliance mark). Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct assembly/
 test-bench-equipment control), permanent equipment-actuate block,
 permanent safety-certification-authority block (this actor never
 self-issues an electric-lighting-equipment safety compliance mark),
 independent equipment verification/registration before maintenance
 scheduling, independent batch verification/registration before
 shipment coordination, independent shipment-quantity recompute
 against the batch's own logged production quantity, double-schedule
 guard, product-type validation, dielectric (hipot/withstand)
 safety-test-voltage plausibility validation, and defect-rate
 plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging (electrical-safety/
 photobiological-hazard/UL-CE-compliance concern) ALWAYS escalates to
 a human plant supervisor; `:log-production-batch` is the only op
 eligible to auto-commit, and only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
